<title>POLAND: Novita surges after subsidiary stake sale.</title>
<headline>Novita surges after subsidiary stake sale.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish carpet maker Novita SA surged 9.5 percent in moderate trade to 11.5 zlotys after announcing it had sold a 10.5-percent stake in a subsidiary to Armstrong Enterprises Inc., analysts said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's because Novita sold the stake, and the strong buying after price suggests the stock will extend gains,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>The subsidiary, retail trader Novita Market SA, went for 3.2 million zlotys, and Novita said Armstrong could up its stake to 30 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
